      "run": "run/api-lifecycle-JAVA-6",
      "kind": "packaged_fixture_failure",
      "summary": "25 tests ran; 24 passed, including five actual API and five upstream chunk cycles. A healthy native PG board fixture failed because an unrelated CEE callback fault globally cleared native CEE results.",
      "correction": "Publish fresh results with scoped unavailable nodes and branch currents; preserve healthy CEE gameplay, meters and wire heating while isolating rejected circuits.",
      "resolution_status": "corrective_change_implemented; final_frozen_acceptance_required",
      "backend": "JAVA"
    },
    {
      "log": "build/api-scoped-NATIVE-10.log",
      "run": "run/api-scoped-NATIVE-10",
      "kind": "packaged_fixture_failures",
      "summary": "27 tests ran; 24 passed. Failures identified a diagnostic identity-size expectation, a native capacitor baseline captured before the already accepted frame's gameplay commit, and an old saved wire entering a native replacement during delayed wire loading.",
      "correction": "Capture the accepted native property history before injecting next-frame failure; preserve strict exact checks on property and device history. Align bounded diagnostic identity reporting. Retire saved extension wire ownership before delayed entity attachment to a native replacement. Review also identified and corrected unavailable-result propagation into the native wire hazard cache.",
      "resolution_status": "corrections_in_progress; final_frozen_acceptance_required",
      "backend": "NATIVE"
    },
    {
      "log": "build/api-complete-NATIVE-11.log",
      "run": "run/api-complete-NATIVE-11",
      "kind": "packaged_fixture_failure",
      "summary": "29 tests ran; 28 passed. Exact native CEE capacitor rollback, externally driven capture isolation, healthy native/public measurements, diagnostic bounds and delayed replacement tests passed. The actual PG multimeter's CEE-wire path still read the previous native result during the same frame as a new callback rejection.",
      "correction": "Check current read-only terminal acceptance before using cached native CEE wire results. Native multimeter number, text and pointer queries also consult current acceptance so they cannot expose a cached powered value before the next inventory update.",
      "resolution_status": "corrective_change_implemented; final_frozen_acceptance_required",
      "backend": "NATIVE"
    },
    {
      "log": "build/api-no-geometry-cold-NATIVE-12.log",
      "run": "run/api-complete-NATIVE-11",
      "archive_prefix": "runs/api-no-geometry-cold-NATIVE-12/",
      "kind": "packaged_cold_restart_failure",
      "summary": "A genuine fresh-JVM cold replacement failed before any API geometry holder existed: an old saved PG wire migrated to the native replacement during delayed entity loading. This run reused the preceding run's runtime directory; its current logs are archived separately to preserve both original failures.",
      "correction": "Persist exact PG PartId and compatibility CEE wire UUID ownership independently of geometry holders. Freeze old-owner IDs before replacement wiring, retire exact old IDs after delayed native loading, and give physically reconnected CEE wires fresh persisted identities. Verify both wire systems with separate-JVM setup and restart fixtures.",
      "resolution_status": "corrective_change_implemented; final_frozen_acceptance_required",
      "backend": "NATIVE"
    },
    {
      "log": "build/api-full-NATIVE-13.log",
      "files": [
        "run/api-full-NATIVE-13/packaged-2026-10-11T10-05-07.960145Z.json"
      ],
      "kind": "packaged_wire_thermal_failure",
      "summary": "31 tests ran; 30 passed, including five actual API and five upstream chunk cycles and actual nonthrowing backend rejection. The custom CEE callback fault fixture passed exact history rollback, healthy scoped publication and same-frame meter rejection, then failed its combined selected-wire/finite-temperature assertion.",
      "correction": "A source-level regression reproduces pinned CEE's cached ordinal lookup returning an unrelated rejected node after builder ordering changes, sending NaN into a healthy native wire's thermal input. Validate cached ordinal hints against stable node identity in compatibility results. The gameplay fixture now verifies its initial wire selection/temperature and reports selection, physical wire and temperature failures separately. A packaged rerun is required to establish whether this fixes the observed failure. This runtime directory was reused for cold verification; only the completed setup build log and its exact setup manifest are retained here, rather than later overwritten latest.log files.",
      "resolution_status": "source_regression_reproduced; packaged_confirmation_pending; final_frozen_acceptance_required",
      "backend": "NATIVE"
    }
